  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IDF Capacity Deveopment for Evidence-Based Land &amp; Agricultural Policy Making in Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of this project is to improve the capacity for evidence-based policy making in Ukraine in the areas of agriculture and land.  The proposed project will upgrade the capacity for evidence-based policy making in the Ministry of Agriculture of Ukraine (MoA)comma State Service of Ukraine for Geodesycomma Cartography and Cadaster (GeoCadastre) and other Government agencies (including the Cabinet of Ministers and the State Registry) and among key stakeholders in the field of agriculture and land governance. In particularcomma the project will (i) Provide MoAcomma GeoCadastre and other Government agencies with analytical support to develop evidence-based policy frameworks and champion them in stakeholder dialogues on key policy issues related to agricultural component of country&apos;s Economic Reform Strategy 2015-20; (ii) Upgrade the capacity of the State Land Cadastercomma State Register and State Statistics to produce and publish the data on land markets and agricultural performance based on their existing raw data; and (iii) Upgrade the capacity of public and private sector players to draw out implications from the existing empirical evidence and design investment projectscomma laws and regulations which are better planned to achieve strategic goals and better monitored to achieve course corrections in priority areas of agriculture and land use.</narrative>
  </description>
